# UI Polishing & PR Workflow Protection Plan

The current Docker container is crashing on startup with an `exec ./entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory` error due to Windows CRLF line-endings. Additionally, the user reported "broken images" (likely icon or glassmorphism clipping) and requested a PR approval system for production.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **GitHub Branch Protection:** I recommend enabling "Require pull request reviews before merging" on GitHub for the `main` branch. This enforces that code MUST be reviewed and tested on the `test` branch before hitting Production.

> [!WARNING]
> **Docke Line-Endings:** I will convert all `.sh` scripts to Unix (LF) to prevent Docker from crashing. This will fix the `Restarting (255)` status on your server.

## Proposed Changes

### [FIX] Docker & Connection
- **[MODIFY] [entrypoint.sh](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/entrypoint.sh)**: Convert to LF line-endings to avoid "no such file" errors in Linux containers.
- **[MODIFY] [main.py](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/main.py)**: Standardize internal container port to **8000** (inherited from Dockerfile EXPOSE) to resolve the mismatch where the app was trying to listen on the Host's 9600 port.

### [FIX] UI Imagery & Icons
- **[MODIFY] [style.css](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/static/style.css)**: Fix icon clipping and ensure Bootstrap Icons (BI) are rendering correctly over the glassmorphism backgrounds.
- **[MODIFY] [dashboard.html](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/templates/dashboard.html)**: Add fallback icons for any sections where imagery is missing or broken (verified: none actually exist in `/static`, so icons are the priority).

### [MODIFY] [deploy.ps1](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/deploy.ps1)
- Add a safety check: Prevent pushing to `main` if the current branch's `test` deployment hasn't been confirmed (local prompt).

## Verification Plan

